      "content": "The image of the perfect child you hold isn't a shield; it's a cage that keeps you from seeing the real, flawed, and deeply human person they actually love. You are not a failure because you are not the version of yourself they imagined, but because you are still here, still trying, and still worthy of their love regardless of your grades or your achievements. The version of you that stayed intact would never have had to face this pain because it never existed in the first place.",
